-- Standard data at a p-adic place: stability, and p-adic bounds passed from
-- theta products to the jets of standard data; scaled jets of standard data
-- are integral; theta kernels with integrally scaled standard data do not
-- raise p-adic gauges.
-- Source: grh-compact/src/New/Curve/ConjugatesOfJets.lean ("This file:
-- Standard data: stability, and p-adic bounds transfer from theta products
-- to their jets. Scaled jets of standard theta data are integral at every
-- prime. One theta lift raises valuations by the bound on jets of standard
-- data."; finHeisOp_mem_standardData, norm_jetSeries_le,
-- norm_jet_jetSeries_le_one, mem_raises_of_dvd).
-- Encoding. Standard data and κ₀ are those of GRH.Proof.Curve.IntegralVacuum
-- (κ₀ an argument k with VacuumScaleOf); the scale per is jetScale(P, Z, s)
-- for the period choice Z. A ℂ-linear form on power series is a linear map
-- on the coordinate module of the monomials. The theta kernel and its
-- gauge bound (Kernel.raises) are FORWARD (ThetaKernelRaises,
-- GRH.Proof.Forward.Theta); the datum of the kernel lives on a standard
-- space V (the source's Hom(I_n, I_{n′})). Not stated here:
-- omega_mem_standardData, pairWeil_mem_standardData (ω(1, g) of the
-- unitary group on standard data), Kernel.smul_mem_raises,
-- mem_raises_of_jet_bound, mem_raises_of_standardData (steps of
-- mem_raises_of_dvd through the Schur jets), and
-- exists_semilinear_isJetConjugate (σ-semilinear conjugation of jets;
-- its consequence for this proof is JetConjugateBound.exists).
-- Part of the GRH blueprint (layer 5, the argument).
